@Help lump editor
In this help lump editor, you can edit help lumps which can be accessed by
scripts using the !- and #HELP commands, and by the HELP instruction.

The .HLP suffix will automatically be added to any lumps you create.

Once you create one, you can edit it using the text editor. This help
lump can contain a limited subset of the commands available in scripts:

  @name
  text
  $text
  :label
  !label;text
  !-help;text

The label referenced by a link can be another label within the same help
file, in which case it will move the cursor to that position when that
link is selected.

